-- The latest versions' notes, for the "What's new" window (Map/News.lua), from CHANGELOG.md.
-- Generated by tools/changelog/build.py; regenerate rather than edit.

local _, ns = ...

ns.MapChangelog = {
	{ version = "Unreleased", date = "", heads = { [1] = "Fixed", }, items = {
		"|cff6e2c0aPlace names whole in other languages|r (#377): where two zones meet, a name longer than the English one went under the zone next to it (\"Acampamento Taurajo\" lost its first letters under Mulgore, and \"Fortaleza da Guardanorte\" and \"Platô do Vigia dos Céus\" didn't show at all, on the Brazilian Portuguese client), and one at a zone's edge faded with it (\"Charco de Lodo\" at the Barrens' top). Each zone's names now stay whole over its neighbours, in the 20 zones where that happened. Done for Brazilian Portuguese so far (it needs that language's art). By cscoder69.",
		"|cff6e2c0aA capital's name banner whole over its map in other languages|r: on a client not in English, the city's own map, coming in as you zoom, covered the zone's banner for it (Thunder Bluff showed only the last letter of \"Penhasco do Trovão\"). The banner is now drawn over the city in your language, and goes as you close in, as it does in English. By cscoder69.",
		"|cff6e2c0aNo bits of neighbours' names in other languages|r: a zone's map letters its neighbours' names round its land, and the map leaves those out, but only as long as the English ones. The longer names showed their ends (\"Flo… P…\" of \"Floresta de Pinhaprata\" by Tirisfal, \"Eira dos Montes\", \"Floresta do Crepúsculo\", \"Estepes Ardentes\"). They're now left out whole, in 33 zones, for Brazilian Portuguese so far. By cscoder69.",
		"|cff6e2c0aOrgrimmar's map fades out at its gate|r: up close, the city's map ended in a straight line across the foot of its gate, where its art stops. It now fades out inside the art's edge, as Ironforge's does. By cscoder69.",
	} },
	{ version = "v0.8.13", date = "2026-11-22", heads = { [1] = "Fixed", [8] = "Improved", [10] = "Known issue", }, items = {
		"|cff6e2c0aPlaces you've explored show on the map|r: the map read what you'd explored as it was built at login, maybe before the game had sent it, and then only when the game said something new was explored. It reads it again as the map first opens and after you enter a new subzone (#422, #410).",
		"|cff6e2c0aNo lag zooming with Show places to explore on|r: every zone you'd looked at kept its outlines, thousands of lines laid out again on every frame of each zoom and pan, nine times the map's own. Only the zones in view and a few recent ones keep them now (#411, #413, #419).",
		"|cff6e2c0aNo stack overflow as the map closes|r with Show places to explore on and Keep warm (#414).",
		"|cff6e2c0aPlaces to explore count what you've already explored|r: it read the map's own record, which can be from before the game sent your exploring after login; it asks the game now, and again as you explore (#417, #418, the Barrens showed 3 of 25).",
		"|cff6e2c0aThe map's art ready before it opens, in more cases|r (keep-warm round you, v0.8.12): the art round you is warmed again each time the map closes (closed on another place, the next opening, centred on you, came in cold); in a cave or another small map its zone is warmed (nothing was); and in a big zone its own art comes first, the farther tiles last (they filled the 400 files and left it out). By cscoder69.",
		"|cff6e2c0aThe map closed in a fight reopens where you left it|r: it reopened on the view from before the fight.",
		"|cff6e2c0aOpening the map after you've moved is lighter with Show places to explore on|r: only zones where you've explored something since are drawn again, not all of them.",
		"|cff6e2c0aClose-up map performance|r: with minimap detail on and unexplored areas hidden, the map draws fewer masked fragments and skips the ones outside the view. By benjaminrobinet.",
		"|cff6e2c0aSupporting OpenMap|r: the foot of What's new's Credits page has a link to copy, for those who'd like to.",
		"Opening the map in a fight can print \"Interface action failed because of an AddOn\" once a session. It's harmless: the map, the quest log and the tracker all work; only the quest log's controller navigation marks are skipped for that one refresh.",
	} },
	{ version = "v0.8.12", date = "2026-11-21", heads = { [1] = "New", [2] = "Improved", [10] = "Fixed", }, items = {
		"|cff6e2c0aShow places to explore|r (the map's menu and Options, off until turned on): for each zone's Explore achievement, the places you haven't explored yet, each with a soft gold outline of the ground that explores it (read from the game's own terrain) and a pin where to go; its tooltip names the place and the achievement's progress. Further out, each zone shows how many places it has left.",
		"|cff6e2c0aThe map works in a fight|r: since v0.8.11 the map stood still in combat (the game's map can't be moved by an addon then without breaking the quest tracker, #345). In a fight OpenMap's map now moves onto frames of its own, over the game's, which is left as it is: zoom, drag, click and resize it as usual, with your arrow, your party and raid, your quests and their areas, the name of the place under the cursor, Questie's and other addons' map icons, and Ctrl-click's waypoint. As the fight ends it all goes back on the game's map, where you left it (#386, #389). (New files: restart the game after updating, a /reload isn't enough.)",
		"|cff6e2c0aUnexplored land darkens as one, the same at every zoom|r (Unexplored areas: Darken): in a zone you've been to, the unexplored parts were darker where the game's map pieces overlap, a different shade once the minimap's detail came in, and could jump between the two as you zoomed. Each piece's share of the darkening is now worked out ahead of time so that, whichever pieces you've explored, the rest come to one even shade, drawn over the map and the minimap alike (#317). By wealdly.",
		"|cff6e2c0aGerman reads better|r: missing German texts filled in and others reworded, in the game's own terms. By gOOvER.",
		"|cff6e2c0aRight-click can be left to other addons|r: Options' \"Right-click zooms out\" (on, as before) turned off leaves right-click on the map to the map and other addons, such as Questie's objectives (#117).",
		"|cff6e2c0aColour matching says what it costs|r: below 100% the ready-made zone tiles aren't used, and its description now says so (#29).",
		"|cff6e2c0aThe map's art ready before it opens|r: the art round you is read in while the map is closed, a few files a frame and out of combat, once the map is built after a login or a /reload and again when you reach a new zone. At a session's first opening, and after travelling, it used to come in over a moment (the files held from the last opening were another place's, or none). The part of the view still fading in as you closed the map is held too. By cscoder69.",
		"|cff6e2c0aThe game's map-pin button works on the stitched map|r: armed, a click on the map drops your pin there, as on the game's own map (#324). By gOOvER.",
		"|cff6e2c0aYour arrow, bigger if you like|r: Options' \"Arrow size\" (100% as before) and \"Your arrow over everything\", which lifts OpenMap's arrow over every icon on the map (#329). By gOOvER.",
		"|cff6e2c0aNo stutter when the map opens|r: since v0.8.11 every set of icons was laid out twice as the map opened, for the whole world and then for your view; once now, as in v0.8.10 (#293, measured by protella: the opening 384 ms to 45).",
		"|cff6e2c0aA resized window keeps its view|r: since v0.8.11 dragging the window's corner zoomed the map out to the whole continent; the place you were looking at stays put now, at the same scale.",
		"|cff6e2c0aYour position read safely everywhere|r: the map, dungeon entrances, flight routes and the controller view all read where you are the same careful way, so a hidden position in combat or in a restricted instance can't raise a Lua error. By gOOvER.",
		"|cff6e2c0aA dungeon's map fills the screen when maximized|r: going from the quest log (L) to the maximized map (M) inside a dungeon left its map small in the middle (#297). By gOOvER.",
		"|cff6e2c0aThe Stockade's entrance opens its map|r: clicking it found neither the game's dungeon map nor its Dungeon Journal page (#289). By gOOvER.",
		"|cff6e2c0aA map window saved off the screen comes back|r: dragged out of reach, it opens where Blizzard puts it again (/openmap reset does the same at any time) (#375).",
		"|cff6e2c0aNo Lua error from the cursor's coordinates|r over a part of the map with no zone of its own, as on retail's maps outside the stitched world (#343).",
		"|cff6e2c0aExplored land keeps its detail up close with Hide unexplored areas|r: zoomed in where the minimap's detail comes in, land you'd explored near an unexplored part (Redridge, Tarren Mill and others) got the painted map back over it, as if unexplored. Only the unexplored parts' own shapes are hidden now (#166, #156, #163, #247, #279, #370).",
		"|cff6e2c0aAppear Offline keeps your place to yourself|r: with Battle.net's Appear Offline on, OpenMap sends your friends and guild nothing (not your place, not even a hello), and tells them to stop showing where you were (#395).",
		"|cff6e2c0aQuestie's quest icons over a town's icons|r: a quest under a vendor, trainer or flight master's icon was hidden; Questie's quests now go over every icon of OpenMap's (#393).",
		"|cff6e2c0aNo \"newer OpenMap\" notice from test builds|r: a test build or a beta no longer tells others it's a newer version; only releases do.",
		"|cff6e2c0aThe windowed quest log sits beside the map|r: it covered part of the map until the window was laid out again; and a window resized by its corner stays on the screen (#327). By gOOvER.",
		"|cff6e2c0aThe right wing's map in Dire Maul, Scarlet Monastery and Blackrock Spire|r: the wing is worked out from the dungeon finder and the area you're in, or the portal you came through, and kept over a /reload; Dungeon Journal is told it too. By puschie286.",
		"|cff6e2c0aCtrl-click left to the game is followed|r: with \"Ctrl-click drops a pin\" off, the game's own waypoint was set on the map underneath (often the continent's), where the game has no route to it, so it was never followed; it's put on the zone under the cursor now, at the cursor, and followed (#19).",
		"|cff6e2c0aCoordinates clear of the border full screen|r: the labels sat under Blizzard's border at the map's bottom edge when the map was maximized (#399).",
	} },
	{ version = "v0.8.11", date = "2026-11-20", heads = { [1] = "Improved", [4] = "Fixed", [15] = "Also", }, items = {
		"|cff6e2c0aTold when a newer OpenMap is out|r: when a friend, guild member or group member has a newer release, a line in chat says so, once a session (\"OpenMap X is out (you have Y). Update through CurseForge.\"). Your version rides only on messages OpenMap already sends them (the hello to friends who use it, your first shared place to your guild, a pin share to your group); older copies pass over it. Options' \"Say when OpenMap has an update\" turns it off, and then your version isn't sent either.",
		"|cff6e2c0a\"The game's map\" on a dungeon's map|r: inside a dungeon, a button at the top of OpenMap's dungeon map switches to the game's own map there, and says how to turn OpenMap's back on (menu > Dungeons) (#371).",
		"|cff6e2c0aA smoother map on a Russian client|r: the zones' art from further out is drawn from tiles baked from the ruRU client's own maps, place names and city banners in Russian, as on an English or a Brazilian Portuguese client (it was every zone's art drawn live). (New textures: restart the game.) By Danpiel.",
		"|cff6e2c0aThe quest tracker keeps working in combat with OpenMap|r: clicking a tracked quest, or opening the map, in a fight gave \"Interface action failed because of an AddOn\", and the objective tracker then stopped updating until you collapsed and opened it again. OpenMap no longer puts its own code in place of the game's map functions (it runs after them), and changes nothing of the game's map in a fight: the map opened in combat is the game's view of it, and OpenMap's comes back as the fight ends (#345, #347, #368).",
		"|cff6e2c0aForever City Labels' pins show on the stitched map|r: its service, profession and class trainer pins were drawn under OpenMap's art. By marquesm91.",
		"|cff6e2c0aNo more green squares over the map|r where the game can't find OpenMap's map tiles (not installed, or the game not restarted since an update): such a tile is left out, and with several missing the map is drawn without them. /openmap status says how many (#349, #353).",
		"|cff6e2c0aTranslations of the ClassicUI Forever question read right again|r: in every language they showed as garbled letters (Ð’ ...).",
		"|cff6e2c0aQuest icons show the quest's level on every map|r: zoomed out, or over the next zone, OpenMap's own quest icons had only the quest's name on their tooltip. They now read as Blizzard's own quest icons do, with the level and its difficulty colour (\"[39+] The Crown of Will\"). By Rambomst.",
		"|cff6e2c0aSharper at the middle zooms|r: between a continent and a zone filling the view, the zones' art was drawn from tiles stretched past their pixels for a while; the zones' own art takes over sooner now. And unexplored land no longer flickers as the zones' art comes in while you pan. By wealdly.",
		"|cff6e2c0aRoogug where he is now|r: in Razorfen Kraul he stands in the middle of the dungeon past the rope bridge (needed for the warriors' Fire Hardened Mail); his pin was at his old spot (#318).",
		"|cff6e2c0aWith Soften on, unexplored land stays darkened up close|r: from Soften's zoom until the minimap came in, a partly explored zone's unexplored land went nearly bright, and flickered back each time the map moved. By wealdly.",
		"|cff6e2c0aThe controller map opens where you set it|r: with the Gamepad UI, \"When reopening the map\" (center on you, keep the zoom, your zone, remember) was only used the first time the map opened; after that it opened wherever it was last left. It's used every time now.",
		"|cff6e2c0aPlace names under the controller's cursor|r: the zone (with its levels) or the area under the cursor is named at the top of the map, as it is under the mouse. Blizzard's own label, which named places on its map hidden under OpenMap's, is hidden while OpenMap's map is up.",
		"|cff6e2c0aQuest areas on the controller map|r: pointing at a quest's icon shades its area, as Blizzard's map does for its own icons, and the area stays in place while zooming. The focused quest's icon is Blizzard's gold one, and its area stays shown when the cursor isn't on another quest. By kr0ozin.",
		"I've also made OpenGroup, a group finder that shows groups from every shard. It's in beta and gets more useful the more people use it. Search OpenGroup on CurseForge.",
	} },
	{ version = "v0.8.10", date = "2026-11-16", heads = { [1] = "Fixed", [16] = "Improved", }, items = {
		"|cff6e2c0aThe map loads again for everyone|r: for some players since v0.8.9 the map opened blank, with an error about GetMapInfoAtPosition. A view worked out while the map was still 0 px across (a divide by zero) was put into the map, and every view after it was worked out from it, so the map stayed blank. A view that isn't one is never put up now, the map's last view and its saved window place and size are checked as they're read back, and a bad one is forgotten (#260, #261, #263). The cause, found by OlehPetrykUA: v0.8.9 put the map together during its very first build, before it had a size.",
		"|cff6e2c0aFewer hitches zooming out|r: the first zoom out of a session made the lettering of every continent and sea name (hundreds of font strings) in one frame; one name is made a frame now. And the tiles fading in as you zoom out set their opacity in 8 steps instead of on every frame, a third to a half fewer calls to the client for a zoom out. By k4m1.",
		"|cff6e2c0aNo more flight paths at Eastern Plaguelands' towers|r: Plaguewood, Northpass, Eastwall and Crown Guard Tower are in the game's flight tables, but no character can learn them and no flight master stands there; they're left out (#264).",
		"|cff6e2c0aA dungeon you've been inside counts as found|r (\"Only places you've found\"): Blackfathom Deeps' entrance, under the Zoram Strand's water, never showed, done or not. Counted from your next visit (#256).",
		"|cff6e2c0aA quest from the quest log shows its map with \"Center on player, keep zoom\"|r: in your own zone the map opened at the kept zoom on you, the quest off screen; it shows the quest's map whole now, as with the other choices (#255).",
		"|cff6e2c0aThe zone highlight toggle works again|r: with it off, zones could still glow under the cursor, where the game made its highlight after OpenMap set the map up (#262).",
		"|cff6e2c0aThe map in combat|r: opened, zoomed or panned in a fight, the map no longer comes up stretched, half empty and see-through until the fight ends. The game can refuse OpenMap's zoom then (the map holds the group members' protected icon); the map is now drawn at the zoom the game kept, and the one you asked for is put up as the fight ends. The window is no longer moved, sized or scaled in a fight either (each was an \"action blocked\"): that waits for the fight's end too (#294). By Vennomfang.",
		"|cff6e2c0aClassicUI Forever|r: its World map option lays the map window out itself every frame, so OpenMap's resize corners and title bar did nothing, and in a fight parts of the map went missing. OpenMap now asks once whether to turn that option off (a reload). Kept on, OpenMap's corners, title bar and saved place stand down and leave the window to it.",
		"|cff6e2c0aStuck on a dungeon's map|r: inside a dungeon, Esc closed the whole map, and it opened on the dungeon again, never the world. Esc (out of combat), a right-click and Back now go to the world map around the dungeon's entrance (or your last place outdoors), and another addon laying the window out again no longer throws the map back to the dungeon.",
		"|cff6e2c0aYour settings kept|r: for some players every setting went back to its default at each login since v0.8.9. A broken number from the blank map (#261) was saved with them, which the game can't read back, so the whole file was lost; such a number is never saved now (#306).",
		"|cff6e2c0a\"Share where you are\" off means off|r: your place could still go out once, queued just before you turned it off or in answer to a friend's hello at that moment. Nothing is sent now while it's off; friends and guild see only your zone, as the game's own lists show it (#277).",
		"|cff6e2c0aLearned flight paths are this character's|r: a new character was shown flight masters another character had learned, and a learned one could show as not learned. Once you've opened a flight master's map on a character, what it lists is what counts (#274, #301).",
		"|cff6e2c0aMount Hyjal's two flight masters|r (Summit of Eternity, Tainted Foothills) are on the map (#288). And the wind riders shown at Eastern Plaguelands' towers, where there are none, are gone (#307, #309).",
		"|cff6e2c0aLearned flight masters in green|r: they were your faction's icon, red for the Horde, which read as not learned. They're the game's flight map green now, greyed where not learned.",
		"|cff6e2c0aThe world map reopens where you left it inside a dungeon|r: with any reopen choice but Always remember, browsing the world map in a dungeon and opening it again went back to the whole continent each time. With nowhere to centre on, it reopens where you left it now.",
		"|cff6e2c0aA dungeon's map never covers your quest log|r: beside the quest log it always opens on your quests; the dungeon's panel shows only when you pick its tab. And |cff6e2c0adungeon maps inside dungeons can be turned off|r (Options and the menu's Dungeons): off, the map opened inside a dungeon is the game's own there; a dungeon's map still opens from its entrance. The first dungeon you're in says once where that switch is. With Dungeon Journal or NeedRoll installed, their map is left to them inside a dungeon (#302, #267).",
		"|cff6e2c0aSharp map by default|r: Soften and paper grain is off for everyone (turn it back on in Look > Up close). It softened the map a moment after it stopped moving, sharp while zooming or panning, which read as the map going blurry (#286, #118). Its tooltip now says so.",
		"|cff6e2c0aThe game's own frame rate limit while the map is open|r: v0.8.9's 60 fps cap held the whole game at 60 while the map was open, below what many had set. It's off by default again (set once back to off for everyone who had 60); the Map frame rate cap is still there to turn on (#273).",
		"|cff6e2c0aFaster loading|r: the stitched map is no longer built during the loading screen. It's built a few seconds after it, a few milliseconds a frame (not in combat), so the map is ready by the time you open it; opened sooner, the rest is built then. By Vennomfang.",
		"|cff6e2c0aA smoother map on a Brazilian Portuguese client|r: the zones' art from further out is drawn from tiles baked from the ptBR client's own maps, place names and city banners in Portuguese, as an English client's has been (it was every zone's art drawn live: panning at mid zoom took about half the frame time). Other languages draw it live as before, until their own tiles are baked. (New textures: restart the game.) By cscoder69, with thanks to developer-felipe, whose #265 took this on first.",
		"|cff6e2c0aLess work while the map is closed|r: the guild and friends lists are read at most every 30 seconds (a raid's roster changes came each time), exploring somewhere recolours the map's art the next time it opens rather than then, and another addon loading no longer looks through every global table again.",
		"|cff6e2c0aSmoother panning and zooming|r: darkened unexplored land lets go of zones out of view (they were laid out on every frame, more the more of the world you'd seen), and of a zone's old shading when it's made again; the boat and zeppelin routes' finer dots are hidden, not only faded, from afar; the continents' names rest their outer glow while the map moves; and the close-up minimap, the cursor's place name and the coordinates skip work when nothing has changed. By cscoder69.",
		"|cff6e2c0aSmoother with the map open|r: \"Quests from every zone\" asked the game for the quests of every zone and city in a single frame, half a second after each opening and again after each burst of quest log updates while the map was open (and once more after it closed). The zones are now read a few a frame and the icons put up together once all are in; nothing is read while the map is closed. /openmap status says what the last reading cost. By Merryfett.",
	} },
	{ version = "v0.8.9", date = "2026-11-14", heads = { [1] = "New", [4] = "Improved", [9] = "Fixed", }, items = {
		"|cff6e2c0aHide world markers in instances|r (the menu's On the map tab, and Options; off unless turned on): in dungeons, raids and battlegrounds, OpenMap's friends, guild, transport and all-zone quest markers step aside. With Dungeon maps off and another addon's dungeon map shown over the world (NeedRoll's), the world under it stops answering the mouse, and a right-click brings the world map back, at the dungeon's outdoor entrance (#232). By HonzoNebro.",
		"|cff6e2c0aPin options|r (OpenMap's options, Moving about and Sharing): - |cff6e2c0aFollow new pins|r: on by default, as before. Off, a pin you drop doesn't become the waypoint, so addons that route to it (Shortest Path Forever) are left alone; the pin's Follow still sets it. - |cff6e2c0aSend new pins to group|r: a pin you drop goes to your party or raid once its card is closed. - |cff6e2c0aAuto-add group's pins|r: pins your party or raid shares are added without asking. By diegodiaz1256.",
		"|cff6e2c0aA map of Blackmaw Hold|r, drawn by Santiago Reyes: all six of its floors, from Blackmaw Grove and the Festering Grotto down to the Depths of Forbidden Magic (the floor list at the top of the dungeon's map, or its arrows). (New textures: restart the game.)",
		"|cff6e2c0aCity of Dalaran's map is Santiago Reyes's updated version, with the Underbelly|r, where the dungeon starts, as a second floor (#220). Opened inside the dungeon, the map shows the floor you're on.",
		"|cff6e2c0aShaper's Terrace's map is Santiago Reyes's final version, with the Prismatic Talus|r as a second floor.",
		"|cff6e2c0aThe controller view's switch in the map's menu too|r: \"OpenMap's map with the Gamepad UI (test)\" is under The map in OpenMap's menu as well as in Options (it was only in Esc > Options > AddOns, and a player took it for gone).",
		"|cff6e2c0aQuestie's quest icons in front|r: a \"!\" or \"?\" is no longer hidden under a flight master or a dungeon's icon; Questie's townsfolk stay under OpenMap's icons (#92).",
		"|cff6e2c0aA word about MapUtils|r: with MapUtils on, OpenMap says once in chat that the two both change the map's zoom, which made the map and Blizzard's quest areas jump while zooming (#160).",
		"|cff6e2c0aOne arrow for you, not two|r: where OpenMap draws your arrow itself (the map underneath can't place you), Blizzard's arrow now steps aside, so the two no longer show a little apart (#229).",
		"|cff6e2c0aQuests from the tracker open on their details|r: the first click on a tracked quest opened the map on the quest list; it shows the quest's text now (#224).",
		"|cff6e2c0aThe map cooler on your graphics card|r: OpenMap's \"Map frame rate cap\" is now 60 by default (and set to 60 once for everyone): a still map was drawn as fast as the card could go (#233). Turn it off in Options if you'd rather.",
		"|cff6e2c0aFade while moving fades while you steer with the mouse|r: the hidden cursor's last place over the map held it solid, so it hardly ever faded (#69).",
		"|cff6e2c0aResizing the window keeps it where it is|r: it could jump to the screen's bottom left (#241).",
		"|cff6e2c0aNighthaven's flight master shows for druids only|r, as only druids can fly from it (#222).",
		"|cff6e2c0aThe controller view takes the mouse too|r (OpenMap's map with the Gamepad UI): the wheel zooms, a drag pans, and a click works as A (left) or X (right) (#234).",
		"|cff6e2c0aCity names in your language|r: Thunder Bluff's and Darnassus' name banners showed in English on other languages' clients; the zone map's own banner, in the client's language, is shown there now (#47).",
		"|cff6e2c0aYour quests' icons show in the controller view|r (Options' \"OpenMap's map with the Gamepad UI\"): there were none, and no tooltips. Every quest in your log is now OpenMap's icon there, at any zoom, in every zone (with \"Quests from every zone\" off: the zone Blizzard's map is on); A tracks the quest and zooms to it. The \"!\" of quests you can start in that zone are there too, with the quest's name on the tooltip. The shaded quest areas aren't on it yet (#225). By k4m1.",
		"|cff6e2c0aZygor's map line stays thick on the stitched map|r: Zygor's route line (and its dots and waypoint icons) shrank to a thin grey line zoomed in and grew far too wide zoomed out, as Zygor sizes them for Blizzard's zoom range; they now stay the same size on screen at every zoom (#218). By rogeriocamorim.",
		"|cff6e2c0aGilneas shows on every language's client|r: on the Russian and Latin American Spanish clients Gilneas was a solid green square, as the game doesn't have its map's art in those languages (as with the dungeon and cave maps before v0.8.5). OpenMap now brings those tiles itself (#152). Found and tested by XaksFlaX. (New textures: restart the game.)",
		"|cff6e2c0aDungeon level ranges|r: the dungeons' levels on the map are now the ones the game's Group Finder gives (each Scarlet Monastery and Dire Maul wing its own); they were an old level each, five levels wide, and some were far off: Razorfen Kraul showed 24-29 for a dungeon of 29-38 (#201). By ConfusionOrb221.",
